This can all rather be:

```
pldm_msgbuf_extract_p(buf, completion_code);

return pldm_msgbuf_complete_consumed(buf);
```

This needs to be a negative errno value also.

In-fact, if you switch to using `encode_pldm_header_only_errno()`, this sequence becomes the usual error handling:

```
rc = encode_pldm_header_only_errno(PLDM_REQUEST, instance_id, PLDM_FWUP,
				     PLDM_UPDATE_SECURITY_REVISION, msg);
if (rc) {
    return rc;
}
```
